 "summary": "The post-PR surface is minimal and free of compatibility artifacts: definition bodies stay unexposed behind `_def`/`_apply` lemmas, and the characteristic API (closed forms, channel-membership iffs, idempotency/orthogonality/completeness, traces, colour-action commutation, Casimir from both sides) is complete and consistently annotated, with `casimir_genM_apply` correctly left un-simp because `LieModule.casimir_apply` already rewrites its LHS. Only optional gap: no `trace_colorSingletState`, so `colorSingletProj N (colorSingletState N) = colorSingletState N` needs a rewrite with `colorSingletState_def` instead of closing by `simp`.",
